    "note": "Complete permanent Beijing railway station passenger ensemble: monumental north facade, both square clock towers with three-tier glazed Chinese roofs and finials, deep central glazed bays and rounded columns, full lateral wings and corner roof pavilions, two genuine courtyard voids, all mapped canopy bounds represented by open platform-roof wings, and the elevated connector with stairs. Preserve the native forecourt, independent service buildings, streets, rails and urban context. Exterior only; no copied signs, lettering, branding, figurative ornament, people, trains or navigable interior. All architectural heights and grades are original photo-proportioned controls because scoped map families have no numeric height fields. Layer1/2/3 values are retained as map facts, not heights. Closed main floor+.65m and foundation-10m share one unchanged host datum. Wings21.5m,central24.5m,clock finials43.3m,corner roofs27.8m; open canopy centres6.4m/eaves7.8m and connector floor4m/roof7.2m. Preserve open courtyards and rail/sky spaces; no blanket parent or canopy ground floor and no per-part host offsets. One unchanged standard field sample outside the north entrance[-12,-57],48.08290055999999m,defines one common Y=0. Native contact still requires current render review. Preview uses the host terrain sample at the authored base; ground slope, facade azimuth and final site fit remain review items."
